## 5. Adding a New Module

### 1. Create Module File

```zsh
# home/dot_zshrc.d/185-new-tool.zsh
# Description: New tool integration

# Only load if tool exists
if command -v newtool &>/dev/null; then
  export NEWTOOL_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/newtool"
  alias nt="newtool"
  
  # Completions
  if [[ -f "$HOME/.local/share/zsh/site-functions/_newtool" ]]; then
    fpath=("$HOME/.local/share/zsh/site-functions" $fpath)
  fi
fi
```

### 2. Add to Main Template

```go
# In dot_zshrc.tmpl, after 180-tools.zsh
source "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.zshrc.d/185-new-tool.zsh"
```

### 3. Numbering Convention

| Range | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| 000-099 | Environment (must be first) |
| 100-199 | Core shell (zinit, plugins, basics) |
| 200-299 | Profile-specific (work, personal, vps) |
| 300-399 | Feature-specific (AI, monitoring, etc.) |
| 400-499 | Application-specific |
| 900-999 | Finalization (compinit, prompt) |

