## 6. Testing Zsh Config

### Dry Run (Syntax Check)

```bash
# Test template rendering
chezmoi execute-template home/dot_zshrc.tmpl > /tmp/test.zshrc
zsh -n /tmp/test.zshrc  # Syntax check only

# Test with profile data
chezmoi execute-template --data='{"settings":{"profile":"vps"}}' home/dot_zshrc.tmpl | zsh -n
```

### Module Load Test

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env zsh
# test_zsh_modules.zsh

for module in ~/.zshrc.d/*.zsh(N); do
  echo "Testing $module..."
  zsh -c "source $module" 2>&1 | head -5
  if [[ $? -eq 0 ]]; then
    echo "  ✅ OK"
  else
    echo "  ❌ FAILED"
  fi
done
```

